# What GitHub counts in the repository's language bar.
#
# Three small files are left out of it (marked "vendored", which is the mark GitHub honours for
# leaving a file out; they are the site's own), so that the bar shows what the site is written in:
# TypeScript, Rust, CSS, Astro and MDX.
#
# - transition.js has to be plain JavaScript: its text is put into every page's head as it stands,
#   and astro.config.ts allows exactly that text in the content security policy.
# - The two Python scripts trim the typefaces with fontTools, once, when a font changes. They are
#   tools for the fonts, not part of the site.
src/scripts/transition.js linguist-vendored
scripts/trim-fonts.py linguist-vendored
scripts/fraunces-soft.py linguist-vendored
